From 517fe27a2ce7fa8d03aa6705a10ff4422197ff5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: frogro <frank.grootens@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 02:16:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: apple: enable the M1 tunneled prefetch aperture before
 enumeration

The integrated kernel assigns the Radeon prefetchable BARs but leaves the
T8103 PCIe-C CPU prefetch aperture disabled. On the measured J274 setup,
VRAM reads return all ones and PSP KDB loading fails. The successful older
eGPU harness issued PREFMEM_ENABLE through a separate Test55 module; that
step was not part of the consolidated host driver.

Issue the strobe using the owning port mapping after initial link recovery
and before rescanning a restarted tunnel. Restrict it to the existing
T8103 kernel-initialized path. There are no fixed physical addresses,
GPU IDs, extra user options, or changed reset-ACK handling.

The register hypothesis and earlier scoped helper derive from Joshua
Warren's linux-aurora PR188, commit
654075e59744da60d1cdf876048dbf38b588ff3d. This integration was AI-assisted.

Validation: rebuilt the original scoped helper against the exact running
7.2.12-usb4sd4-egpu1 sources/config. VRAM changed from all ones to readable
data immediately after the strobe. After Razer tunnel reauthorization,
PSP and all GPU IP initialization completed, all four drivers bound, IB
ring tests passed, and 1048576 GPU-computed values matched an independent
CPU calculation. The native host object compiles. Fresh boot of the full
kernel with this native hook remains a separate hardware validation.
---
 drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple-pciec.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple-pciec.c b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple-pciec.c
index 8eff70858..3577b8561 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple-pciec.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple-pciec.c
@@ -409,6 +409,23 @@ bool apple_pcie_tunnel_needs_cold_init(struct device_node *np)
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(apple_pcie_tunnel_needs_cold_init);
 
+/*
+ * T8103's prefetchable CPU aperture needs an enable strobe after port
+ * initialization. PCI BAR assignment alone does not enable this path: reads
+ * return all ones and device firmware uploaded through VRAM is not visible.
+ * Do this before downstream drivers probe, including after tunnel restart.
+ * Keep other SoCs and firmware-owned initialization paths unchanged.
+ */
+static void apple_pcie_enable_prefetch_window(struct apple_pcie_port *port)
+{
+	if (!apple_pcie_tunnel_needs_cold_init(port->pcie->dev->of_node))
+		return;
+
+	apple_pcie_port_writel(port, 1, PORT_PREFMEM_ENABLE);
+	/* This is a strobe, not a readable enabled-state bit. */
+	apple_pcie_port_readl(port, PORT_PREFMEM_ENABLE);
+}
+
 /*
  * Prepare T8103 PCIe-C before the tunnel container creates its DART child.
  * macOS traces and the isolated live replay both show that APPCLK and the
@@ -1025,6 +1042,7 @@ static int apple_pcie_tunnel_restart_link(struct apple_pcie_port *port)
 			msleep(100);
 			if (!(apple_pcie_port_readl(port, PORT_LINKSTS) & PORT_LINKSTS_UP))
 				continue;
+			apple_pcie_enable_prefetch_window(port);
 			dev_info(port->pcie->dev, "native tunnel link ready after %d attempt(s)\n",
 				 attempt + 1);
 			return 0;
@@ -1578,6 +1596,7 @@ static int apple_pcie_setup_port(struct apple_pcie *pcie,
 		msleep(100);
 		dev_info(pcie->dev, "initial tunnel recovery wait complete, link %#x\n",
 			 apple_pcie_port_readl(port, PORT_LINKSTS));
+		apple_pcie_enable_prefetch_window(port);
 	}
 
 	return 0;
-- 
